{
  "Small badge beside the product name; labels this page as an interactive demo/sandbox, not a children's playground\u0004playground": "プレイグラウンド",
  "Tooltip on a status dot. 'isReady()' is an API name — keep it verbatim. 'gate UI on this' = show the UI only once it is ready; 'flash-of-untranslated-content' is the technical term for untranslated text briefly showing (FOUC)\u0004isReady() — gate UI on this to avoid flash-of-untranslated-content": "isReady() — 未翻訳コンテンツのちらつきを避けるため、UIをこれで制御します",
  "ready": "準備完了",
  "loading…": "読み込み中…",
  "Heading above the sidebar table-of-contents navigation links\u0004On this page": "このページの内容",
  "Hero tagline (marketing register). 'Angular' is the framework name and 'i18n' the abbreviation for internationalization — keep both. 'signal-first' means built around Angular Signals; render the technical sense, not 'first signal'\u0004Angular i18n, the signal-first way": "Angular i18n、シグナルファーストのアプローチ",
  "Hero subheading (marketing prose). Keep the product/tech names verbatim: 'ng-linguo', 'Angular', 'SignalStore', 'HTML', 'i18n'. 'signals'/'store methods' are Angular Signals concepts; 'read translations'/'change the language' describe data access, not literal reading/writing\u0004ng-linguo is a complete internationalization (i18n) toolkit for Angular, built on a SignalStore. You read translations as signals, change the language through store methods, and your translators never touch a line of HTML. Use the language switcher above and watch every example on this page update instantly.": "ng-linguo は、SignalStore をベースに構築された Angular 向けの完全な国際化 (i18n) ツールキットです。翻訳はシグナルとして読み取り、ストアメソッドを通じて言語を変更でき、翻訳者が HTML コードに触れることはありません。上記の言語スイッチャーを使用して、このページのすべての例が即座に更新されるのをご覧ください。",
  "Highlight title. Means: the English source text itself is used as the translation lookup key (no separate key names)\u0004English is the key": "英語がキーです",
  "Highlight body. 'lookup key' = the value used to find a translation; 'dotted key paths' = names like home.header.title used by other i18n libraries; 'AI model' = an LLM doing the translation\u0004Write real sentences in your components — that text is the lookup key. No dotted key paths to invent or keep in sync, and an AI model always sees full, meaningful context.": "コンポーネントに実際の文章を記述してください — そのテキストがルックアップキーになります。ドット区切りのキーパスを考案したり同期させたりする必要はなく、AI モデルは常に完全で意味のあるコンテキストを認識します。",
  "Highlight title: translation files contain plain text only, no HTML markup\u0004Translators never see HTML": "翻訳者はHTMLを見ません",
  "Highlight body. 'Named slots' = the [name] bracket placeholders; 'Cross-site scripting' = the XSS security vulnerability\u0004Named slots bind to your own templates, so links and bold text render as real Angular while the file stays plain text. Cross-site scripting is impossible by design.": "名前付きスロットは独自のテンプレートにバインドされるため、リンクや太字のテキストは実際の Angular としてレンダリングされ、ファイルはプレーンテキストのままです。クロスサイトスクリプティングは設計上不可能です。",
  "Highlight title: correct grammatical forms (plurals, gender, etc.) in each language\u0004Real grammar, every language": "あらゆる言語で正しい文法",
  "Highlight body. Keep 'ICU MessageFormat 2' verbatim (a standard). 'locale-aware numbers' = numbers formatted per language\u0004ICU MessageFormat 2 handles plurals, ordinals, gender, and locale-aware numbers — Polish gets four plural forms, English gets two, from a single message.": "ICU MessageFormat 2 は、複数形、序数、性別、ロケール対応の数値を処理します。単一のメッセージから、ポーランド語では4つの複数形、英語では2つの複数形が得られます。",
  "Highlight title. 'Additive' = re-running the extractor adds to your files without overwriting existing translations\u0004Additive extraction": "追加抽出",
  "Highlight body. 'extractor' = the CLI that scans source for strings; 'catalogs' = the per-language translation files\u0004Re-run the extractor any time: new and changed strings merge into your catalogs while every existing translation is kept.": "いつでもエクストラクターを再実行できます。新規および変更された文字列はカタログにマージされ、既存の翻訳はすべて保持されます。",
  "Highlight title: translating the app using an AI / LLM\u0004Translate with AI": "AIで翻訳",
  "Highlight body. 'guided command-line tool' = the interactive CLI; 'chat model' = an LLM such as ChatGPT/Gemini/Claude\u0004A guided command-line tool copies a prompt for any chat model, or calls your own AI provider. Adding a whole new language is a single command.": "ガイド付きコマンドラインツールは、任意のチャットモデル用のプロンプトをコピーするか、独自のAIプロバイダーを呼び出します。新しい言語を丸ごと追加するのも、単一のコマンドで完了します。",
  "Highlight title. Keep 'SSR' (server-side rendering) and 'tree-shakeable' (unused code is dropped from the bundle); 'Zoneless' = works without Angular's zone.js\u0004Zoneless, SSR-safe, tree-shakeable": "ゾーンレス、SSRセーフ、ツリーシェイク可能",
  "Highlight body. Keep 'signals' (Angular Signals) and 'zone.js' (Angular library name) verbatim; 'renders on the server' = supports server-side rendering\u0004Reactivity is signals all the way down. No zone.js, it renders on the server, and optional features ship only when you import them.": "リアクティビティはすべてシグナルで構成されています。zone.js は不要で、サーバーでレンダリングされ、オプション機能はインポートされた場合にのみ提供されます。",
  "Section-group label for the first group of examples: installing the library and the three basic ways to translate (the t pipe, the [t] directive, and injectTranslate)\u0004Getting started": "はじめに",
  "Section heading: initial setup / installation of the library\u0004Setup": "セットアップ",
  "Card title. 'translation store' = the ng-linguo SignalStore that holds translations (a noun)\u0004Set up the translation store": "翻訳ストアを設定する",
  "Card body (developer-docs tone, step-by-step). Keep API names verbatim: provideTranslate(), restoreLang(), injectTranslate(). 'persisted → browser → default' is the order restoreLang() chooses the startup language in; 'keyed by' = uses as the lookup key; 'CLI' = the command-line tool\u0004Three steps to a translated app: (1) register the store with provideTranslate() — it never fetches on its own; (2) load a language at startup with restoreLang(), which picks persisted → browser → default; (3) translate with the pipe, directive, or injectTranslate(). Translation files are plain JSON keyed by the original English text — generate them with the CLI shown under Tooling & workflow below.": "翻訳されたアプリを作成するための3つのステップ: (1) provideTranslate() でストアを登録します — ストアが単独でフェッチすることはありません。(2) restoreLang() で起動時に言語をロードします。これは、永続化された言語 → ブラウザの言語 → デフォルトの言語の順に選択します。(3) パイプ、ディレクティブ、または injectTranslate() を使用して翻訳します。翻訳ファイルは、元の英語テキストをキーとするプレーンな JSON です — これらは、以下の「ツールとワークフロー」に示されている CLI で生成します。",
  "Section heading. 'pipe' is the Angular template-pipe concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol 't'\u0004The [code]t[/code] pipe": "[code]t[/code]パイプ",
  "Card title. 'template' = the Angular HTML template\u0004Translate in the template": "テンプレートでの翻訳",
  "Card body. 'lookup key' = the value used to find a translation; the point is that the original English is both what you write and the key. 'never empty' = no blank UI\u0004Write the English text straight into your template — that text is the lookup key. If a translation is missing, the pipe shows the English instead, so the screen is never empty.": "テンプレートに英語のテキストを直接記述してください — そのテキストがルックアップキーになります。翻訳が見つからない場合、パイプは代わりに英語を表示するため、画面が空白になることはありません。",
  "Welcome back!": "おかえりなさい！",
  "Section heading. 'directive' is the Angular directive concept — keep the technical term; [code] wraps the code symbol '[t]'\u0004The [code][[t][/code] directive": "[code][[t][/code]ディレクティブ",
  "Card title. 'element' = an HTML / DOM element\u0004Translate an element": "要素の翻訳",
  "Card body. 'signals' = Angular Signals; 'translation file' = the JSON dictionary; 'directive' = the Angular [t] directive; 'RxJS subscriptions to manage' = manual subscribe/unsubscribe bookkeeping\u0004Put the text on the element itself. The directive watches the store's signals for you, so when a translation file finishes loading the element updates on its own — no RxJS subscriptions to manage.": "テキストを要素自体に配置します。ディレクティブがストアのシグナルを監視するため、翻訳ファイルの読み込みが完了すると要素は自動的に更新されます — RxJS のサブスクリプションを管理する必要はありません。",
  "Card title. 'TypeScript' is the programming language name — keep verbatim\u0004Translate in TypeScript": "TypeScriptでの翻訳",
  "Card body. 'the pipe' = the Angular t pipe; 'TypeScript' = component class code; keep computed() verbatim; 'parameters' = the ICU placeholder values; 'updates automatically' = stays reactive\u0004The pipe's equivalent for TypeScript. Call it inside a computed() and the result updates automatically whenever your parameters or the active language change.": "TypeScript 用のパイプの同等機能です。computed() 内で呼び出すと、パラメーターまたはアクティブな言語が変更されるたびに結果が自動的に更新されます。",
  "Section-group label: examples that rely on ICU MessageFormat — plurals, ordinals, gender selection, and number formatting\u0004Plurals & formatting": "複数形と書式設定",
  "Section heading: grammatical plural forms (one file / many files)\u0004Plurals": "複数形",
  "Card title. 'Counting plurals' = cardinal forms (1 file / 2 files), as opposed to ordinals like 1st/2nd\u0004Counting plurals across languages": "複数言語での複数形の数え方",
  "Card body. one/few/many/other are CLDR plural-category names — keep them in English; 'count' is a variable name (keep); the point is that different languages need a different number of plural forms\u0004English has two forms (one/other); Polish has four (one/few/many/other). You can also give an exact '0' form when 'No new messages' reads better than '0 messages'. Step count through 1, 2, 5, 22 in Polish to watch the form change.": "英語には2つの形式 (one/other) があり、ポーランド語には4つの形式 (one/few/many/other) があります。「0件のメッセージ」よりも「新しいメッセージはありません」の方が自然な場合は、正確な「0」形式を指定することもできます。ポーランド語でカウントを1、2、5、22と進めて、形式の変化をご覧ください。",
  "Section heading: ordinal numbers (1st, 2nd, 3rd …), not cardinal counts\u0004Ordinals": "序数",
  "Card title. 'Ordinal numbers' = ranking forms; keep the 1st/2nd/3rd examples as English ordinal suffixes\u0004Ordinal numbers (1st, 2nd, 3rd …)": "序数 (1st, 2nd, 3rd …)",
  "Card body. st/nd/rd/th are the English ordinal suffixes; one/two/few/other are CLDR category names (keep in English); EN/PL/DE meaning English/Polish/German; '{n}.' shows the number followed by a period\u0004English picks st/nd/rd/th depending on the number (one/two/few/other); Polish and German just add a period, like '{n}.'.": "英語は数値に応じて st/nd/rd/th (one/two/few/other) を選択しますが、ポーランド語とドイツ語は「{n}.」のようにピリオドを追加するだけです。",
  "Section heading. 'select' is the ICU MessageFormat 'select' construct (pick a variant by gender) — not a dropdown and not the verb 'to select'\u0004Gender select": "性別選択",
  "Card title. This demonstrates the ICU 'select' construct: choosing a different sentence depending on a value (here, gender)\u0004Pick the wording by gender": "性別で表現を選択する",
  "Card body. 'pronoun' = she/he/they; 'verb ending' = a verb form that changes with gender (as in Polish); 'matches on count and gender at the same time' = one message that depends on two values at once\u0004English changes the pronoun (she/he/they); Polish changes the verb ending. The second line matches on count and gender at the same time — and every combination can read differently from one language to the next.": "英語は代名詞 (she/he/they) が変化し、ポーランド語は動詞の語尾が変化します。2行目は数と性別に同時に一致し、すべての組み合わせが言語によって異なる読み方になります。",
  "Section heading: locale-aware number formatting (digit-group separators)\u0004Number formatting": "数値の書式設定",
  "Card title. 'Digit grouping' = the separators inside large numbers (1,000 vs 1.000 vs 1 000), which differ by language\u0004Digit grouping per language": "言語ごとの桁区切り",
  "Card body. ':number' is an ICU formatter token (keep verbatim); en/de/pl meaning English/German/Polish; the figures show how each language groups thousands\u0004The :number formatter groups digits the way each language expects: en 1,234,567 · de 1.234.567 · pl 1 234 567.": ":number フォーマッターは、各言語が期待する方法で桁をグループ化します: 英語 1,234,567 · ドイツ語 1.234.567 · ポーランド語 1 234 567。",
  "Section-group label: more advanced translation features — disambiguating identical words by context, and rich text with slot tags\u0004Advanced messages": "高度なメッセージ",
  "Section heading. 'Context' = the translation disambiguation feature (gettext msgctxt); 'homonyms' = words spelled the same but meaning different things\u0004Context (homonyms)": "コンテキスト（同音異義語）",
  "Card title about homonyms / disambiguation\u0004Same word, different meaning": "同じ単語、異なる意味",
  "Card body. 'context' is the ng-linguo option name (keep verbatim); 'key' = lookup key; 'msgctxt' is the gettext technical term (keep); the same English word can map to different translations\u0004A context label becomes part of the key (gettext calls it msgctxt) and also tells the translator which meaning you mean. Switch to Polish to see each one translated differently.": "コンテキストラベルはキーの一部となり (gettext では msgctxt と呼ばれます)、翻訳者には意図する意味を伝えます。ポーランド語に切り替えて、それぞれが異なる翻訳になっていることを確認してください。",
  "audio player\u0004Play": "再生",
  "game\u0004Play": "プレイ",
  "direction\u0004Right": "右",
  "correct\u0004Right": "正しい",
  "sequence\u0004Order": "順序",
  "purchase\u0004Order": "注文",
  "no cost\u0004Free": "無料",
  "available\u0004Free": "空き",
  "Section heading. 'Rich text' = text with links/emphasis; 'slot tags' = the [name] bracket placeholders ng-linguo uses in translations\u0004Rich text (slot tags)": "リッチテキスト（スロットタグ）",
  "Card title. The point: links and styled text appear in the UI, but the translation files stay plain text with no HTML\u0004Links and bold text — with no HTML in your translation files": "リンクと太字のテキスト — 翻訳ファイルにHTMLは不要",
  "Card body. 'named slots' = the [name] bracket placeholders; keep 'ng-template tFor' verbatim; 'real bracket' = a literal [ character; 'XSS' is the web-security term (keep). [[name]…[[/name] is escaped so it shows as the literal text [name]…[/name] — keep the doubled brackets\u0004Translators only ever see named slots like [[name]…[[/name] — never HTML tags. You bind each slot to your own ng-template tFor, so you decide what it renders as: a link, bold text, anything. Need a real bracket in your text? Type the opening one twice. Translated text is never inserted as HTML, so cross-site scripting (XSS) is impossible by design.": "翻訳者は [[name]…[[/name] のような名前付きスロットのみを参照し、HTML タグを見ることはありません。各スロットは独自の ng-template tFor にバインドされるため、リンク、太字のテキストなど、何としてレンダリングするかを決定できます。テキストに実際の角括弧が必要な場合は、開始括弧を2回入力してください。翻訳されたテキストが HTML として挿入されることは決してないため、クロスサイトスクリプティング (XSS) は設計上不可能です。",
  "Onboarding hint. [docs] wraps a link to the documentation — translate the wrapped word too and keep the [docs] tags around it\u0004Read the [docs]documentation[/docs] to get started": "開始するには、[docs]ドキュメント[/docs]をお読みください。",
  "Consent line shown before sign-up. [terms] wraps a link; 'Terms of Service' is the standard name of the legal agreement — use the conventional target-language equivalent\u0004By continuing you agree to our [terms]Terms of Service[/terms]": "続行することで、当社の[terms]利用規約[/terms]に同意するものとします",
  "Warning before a destructive, irreversible action. [warn] wraps the emphasized lead word 'Warning:'\u0004[warn]Warning:[/warn] this action cannot be undone": "[warn]警告:[/warn] この操作は元に戻せません",
  "Demo of ng-linguo's slot syntax and its bracket escape. 'Escaped' is the programming sense (made literal via the [[ escape), not fleeing; 'stays literal' = shown as plain text; 'slot' = a fillable [name] region. [[b]bold[[/b] is escaped literal text, [b]this[/b] is a real slot — keep both forms exactly\u0004Escaped [[b]bold[[/b] stays literal — [b]this[/b] is a slot": "エスケープされた[[b]bold[[/b]はリテラルとして表示されます — [b]これは[/b]スロットです",
  "Consent line with a nested slot. [link] wraps a link to the Terms; [b] emphasizes a word inside it. 'Terms and Conditions' is the standard legal-document name — use the conventional target-language equivalent\u0004Agree to our [link]Terms and [b]Conditions[/b][/link]": "当社の[link]利用[b]規約[/b][/link]に同意する",
  "Section-group label: the surrounding workflow — the ESLint setup and the extract/translate/compile pipeline\u0004Tooling & workflow": "ツールとワークフロー",
  "Section heading. 'ESLint' is a tool name — keep verbatim; 'a11y' is the numeronym for accessibility (keep, or use the target word for accessibility)\u0004ESLint & a11y": "ESLintとa11y",
  "Card title (colloquial). 'accessibility linter' = the ESLint a11y rule; 'keep it happy' = satisfy the rule; '[t]' is a code symbol (keep); 'empty elements' = elements with no text written in the HTML\u0004Keep the accessibility linter happy with empty [t] elements": "空の [t] 要素でアクセシビリティリンターを満足させる",
  "Card body. Keep verbatim: @angular-eslint/template/elements-content, [t]. 'markup' = the HTML you write; 'fallback' = text shown before translations load; 'the hero' = the large heading at the top of the page\u0004Angular's accessibility rule @angular-eslint/template/elements-content warns about empty headings, links, and buttons. A [t] element gets its text at runtime, so you can leave the markup empty — every heading on this page is an empty [t] element, and only the hero keeps its text as a fallback shown before translations load.": "Angular のアクセシビリティルール @angular-eslint/template/elements-content は、空の見出し、リンク、ボタンについて警告します。[t] 要素は実行時にテキストを取得するため、マークアップを空のままにできます — このページのすべての見出しは空の [t] 要素であり、ヒーローセクションのみが翻訳の読み込み前に表示されるフォールバックとしてテキストを保持しています。",
  "Section heading: the build-time CLI pipeline that turns source strings into translated files (extract, translate, compile)\u0004Translation workflow": "翻訳ワークフロー",
  "Card title. 'English source' = the original strings; 'translated files' = the per-language .po/.json files\u0004From English source to translated files": "英語ソースから翻訳ファイルへ",
  "Card body. Keep verbatim: extract CLI, gettext, .po, JSON, ng-linguo, SDK, API key, translator, CI. 'additive' = re-running adds without overwriting; 'guided menu' = the interactive CLI; 'chat model' = an LLM such as ChatGPT/Gemini/Claude; 'merges the reply' = applies the model's response back into the files\u0004The extract CLI scans your source, keeps the strings in standard gettext .po files, and compiles them to the JSON the app loads. Re-running it is additive — new strings merge in, existing translations stay. Run it with no command for a guided menu, or as plain commands in CI. To translate, copy a ready-made prompt into any chat model, or point the translator option at a small module that calls your own AI provider — ng-linguo writes the prompt and merges the reply, and your SDK and API key never leave your machine.": "extract CLI はソースをスキャンし、文字列を標準の gettext .po ファイルに保持し、アプリがロードする JSON にコンパイルします。再実行は追加的であり、新しい文字列はマージされ、既存の翻訳は保持されます。コマンドなしで実行するとガイド付きメニューが表示され、CI ではプレーンなコマンドとして実行できます。翻訳するには、既製のプロンプトを任意のチャットモデルにコピーするか、translator オプションを独自の AI プロバイダーを呼び出す小さなモジュールに指定します — ng-linguo がプロンプトを作成して応答をマージし、SDK と API キーがマシンから離れることはありません。",
  "Page footer. 'ng-linguo' is the product name (keep verbatim); 'living documentation' = documentation that is also a working demo\u0004Built with ng-linguo · this playground is also living documentation.": "ng-linguoで構築 · このプレイグラウンドは生きたドキュメントでもあります。",
